From 71ce0302799f1d3689e82c6e70aea5aeb67616b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:49:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): SNAPBACK flat near-black redesign ported to the
 modular editor

Port the SNAPBACK visual language (uploaded snapback-ui reference) onto the
current component architecture. No parameter IDs, engine, state-format or
routing changes - this is a paint + layout diff plus two small build fixes.

Theme:
- New Source/SnapbackTheme.h: single source of truth for the flat palette
  (#0E0E12 surfaces, #5B7FF0 SNAPBACK blue, #9B6DF0 TRANSIENT violet),
  six per-signal colours, bank accent helpers, trapezoid path helper
- wavelens::ui now aliases snap:: values; layerColour maps to the new
  blue/violet families

Header (PluginHeaderComponent):
- White flat 'S N A P B A C K' wordmark (replaces purple gradient)
- New RESET button (scope + zoom only; samples/parameters untouched)
- Compact BPM cluster (- 120 +) beside retained power/menu/preset/favourite

Scope (MasterWaveformComponent):
- Subtle blue-grey grid, flat near-black background and ruler
- Master M overlay now starts INACTIVE (selected pair on open)
- Trigger line/flash recoloured to SNAPBACK blue

Control strip (WaveformControlBar):
- TRIGGER tab is a SNAPBACK-blue trapezoid (still opens the trigger drawer)
- Split GRID / SECONDS toggle buttons (blue / violet active states)
- Zoom out / live zoom level / zoom in buttons; bar-span combo moved into
  the trigger drawer (SPAN) so no functionality is lost

Sample groups (SampleGroupComponent / SampleSelectorDot / browser):
- Bank-accent headings, 3 blue / 3 violet selector circles, M-styled
  layer enable button; all existing mute/solo/audition/load/clear
  behaviour preserved

Layer editor (LayerEnvelopeComponent):
- 11 parameter tiles (GAIN, PITCH, POGO, TRIM F, TRIM B, FADE IN, FADE OUT,
  TIMING, PAN, HP, LP) in two rows; vertical volume fader converted to the
  GAIN tile on the same layerGain parameter
- HP/LP tiles replace the dual-handle filter bar visually, wired to the
  existing layerHighPass/layerLowPass parameters (DSP untouched)
- Neutral grey-blue waveform (#97A0B4) under a bright bank-accent FL
  envelope; flat panels replace violet chrome

LookAndFeel (SpectralMultipleLookAndFeel):
- Tile slider rendering (label, value, 2px track, bipolar centre fill,
  thumb, width-aware font shrink), trapezoid button background, flat
  buttons/combos/popups

Build fixes needed for JUCE 7.0.12 (current main does not compile):
- SampleSelectorDot / FilterControlComponent inherit SettableTooltipClient
- GAIN textFromValueFunction set after SliderAttachment (attachment
  overwrites it with parameter getText)

Tools:
- Tools/UiSnapshot.cpp + BUILD_UI_SNAPSHOT=ON: headless renderer that
  loads synthetic samples through the real processor and saves PNGs of
  the actual editor at 1280x760 / 1020x620 / 1920x1200

Verified: Linux VST3 builds clean, engine + processor CTest suites pass,
14/14 pixel checks on rendered screenshots at all three sizes.
